*Note on scripting and threading

  GraalVM script engines are created per-thread rather than shared.  This avoids concurrency
  problems — all state is injected into the function — but it does mean memory scales with the
  number of threads.  For validation at the socket boundary, that is bounded by the number of
  CPU cores, so the overhead is modest.



